      "path": "math-tool.ps1",
      "line": 18,
      "body": "The parameters accept every non-negative `Int32`, but these accumulators begin as native integers and the additions eventually widen to `Double`; for example, `N=93` returns an imprecise `1.97402742198682E+19` instead of the exact Fibonacci value `12200160415121876738`. Valid inputs can therefore silently produce incorrect results. Keep the accumulators as `System.Numerics.BigInteger` (or explicitly restrict the accepted range)."
    },
    {
      "id": 4118252311,
      "path": "math-tool.Tests.ps1",
      "line": 60,
      "body": "The helper captures `StdErr`, but the test only checks `StdOut`. A CLI that emits the correct result plus a diagnostic or other incidental message on stderr would still pass, despite the stated no-incidental-output contract. Add an assertion that `StdErr` is null or empty."
    }
  ]
}

